marvel's guardians of the galaxy puts  you in the hover boots of star-lord and  asks you to lead a team of the galaxy's  deadliest heroes you might not get to  control the rest of the guardians  directly but don't be fooled you have to  work as a team in order to make the most  of the game's combat the game loves to  throw all sorts of different terms  attack properties and status effects at  you and while i don't think this is a  particularly difficult game it did take  me a lot longer than i thought it would  to really get the full hang of the  combat which is why i'm here to lay it  all down for you so you'll have more of  a leg up than i did when you start the  game and if you find this helpful please  give a like and sub it helps out a  lot smooth plan so far  hey at least i'm pulling my weight  there's not much weight to pull yes  star-lord may have guns to pupe you with  but it's important to understand that  while they deal damage and are perfectly  capable of taking down lower tier  enemies the real focus is on the  abilities both peters and the rest of  the guardians abilities can do all sorts  of stuff like crowd control multi or  single enemy damage but a key element to  focus on is if it's a damage ability or  a stagger ability damage is exactly what  it sounds like focusing on taking out  large chunks of the enemy's health bar  gamora's starting ability deadly strike  deals heavy damage to a single target  making her your best damage dealer early  in the game however some enemies might  be resistant to gamora's attacks certain  higher tier foes will have a stagger bar  and if you want to take them down  effectively you'll need to fill it using  abilities that cause stagger once full  the enemy will become  staggered which leaves them vulnerable  to previously resisted abilities drax's  starting move destroy deals heavy  stagger so a basic combo would be to use  drax to stagger someone and then have  gamora sweep in with heavy damage  so the key is going to be spending time  learning the role each move serves you  can find all of this information on the  abilities menu memorizing each move  sounds like a lot to handle but each  character only gets 4 moves total  throughout the game and you unlock them  at a slow enough pace so you don't get  overwhelmed also a handy little combat  tip if you forget which move causes  stagger when you pull up the ability  menu in combat stacker moves will always  have the stagger icon on them another  thing you have to consider is elemental  moves over the course of the game peter  gets access to elemental shots on his  blasters these moves are used both in  puzzles as well as combat sometimes the  uses will be pretty obvious like  destroying these enemy shields with your  eye shot but in the heat of battle you  might not be sure how best to use your  elemental attacks thankfully the game  actually makes this pretty easy to the  left of the enemy's health bar is a  square box with an icon which tells you  which type of shot is best effective  standard enemies will have this blaster  icon which means peter's basic attack  works best while special foes will have  icons associated with different elements  now this might all sound really obvious  but the game doesn't explain this and it  actually took me longer than i'd like to  admit to notice this so consider this me  passing these savings on to you  a seemingly minor but important move you  might actually forget about is that  peter has a melee attack typically you  aren't going to be using this all that  much you're better off blasting or using  an ability and you're gonna kind of  forget it's a thing but melee can  actually be pretty effective especially  when peter happens to combo a melee with  other guardians to do more damage and  there are some enemies that are weak to  melee and you can make really short work  of them unfortunately there really isn't  any sort of tell i could find and you  just need to experiment to see which  enemies are weak to melee just give them  a good whack and you'll know right away  if the melee is effective or not okay so  now that you know how to use all your  tools it's time to maximize your damage  certain abilities can apply a damage  multiplier to the enemy as signified by  this icon here  each guardian is capable of applying  their own multiplier meaning you can  stack them on a single enemy up to five  times however getting it this high is  pretty tricky the effect doesn't stay  very long so you'll need to blow all of  your abilities at the same time which  might not even be the best idea for  reasons we'll talk about plus on common  foes you'll likely kill them before  getting all the way to a stack of 5.  i recommend only trying to get higher  stacks on larger boss enemies and for  common encounters focus on just getting  two stacks instead and then lay down the  damage interestingly the game doesn't  communicate to you which abilities apply  a damage multiplier leading to a bit of  guesswork for me it always triggered on  abilities that affect multiple targets  like peter's eye of the hurricane  gamora's shadow strike drax's pound and  pummel rocket's grav stick grenade and  groot entangle when you're juggling all  these different systems stagger  elemental damage multipliers not only  does it dish out the hurt but it also  increases your momentum meter this is  basically the game's way of saying hey  you're doing a good job keep it up aside  from a nice pat on the back the reason  you care about momentum is because  raising it higher will increase your  chances of bonus attack prompts  triggering giving you free damage you'll  also gain a larger xp payout at the end  of a fight momentum will decrease while  being inactive so you want to be laying  down the hurt constantly but repeating  the same moves over and over reduces how  much momentum they give you so you want  to keep mixing up your tactics the worst  thing you can do is spam all 5 guardian  abilities in one go instead try and pace  them out to keep your momentum up this  all sounds like a lot to keep track of  but the good thing is the game layers a  lot of these systems slowly over time  practice each new element as it's  introduced and soon you'll be kicking  ass as a well-coordinated team i'm going  to leave you with some gameplay of  everything i just talked about all  coming together so you can see in action  and remember if you found this video  helpful please why not give a like and  sub it really helps us out and make sure  to stay tuned to gamespot for our full  review of marvel's guardians of the  galaxy  drags  [ __ ] fireworks  oh sucker suck on this yeah hello  time's up  keep them busy crew  okay coast is clear you're up rocket  make it fast of course there ain't a  lock this side of zandar i can't [ __ ] i  am adding to your debt for every extra  minute this takes keep your mannies on  you can't rush genius
 

